A letter of intent is not a build contract.

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:54.700
TSMC's new number is the 4th quarter-guide, $52.3 billion to $54.3 billion, about 14% above

00:01:54.700 --> 00:02:02.660
the 3rd quarter at the midpoint. Net profit rose 68.7% to $763.06 billion new Taiwan

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:11.280
dollars, about $23.55 billion. Revenue was $46.72 billion, above the company's own range

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:20.060
of $44.6 billion to $45.8 billion. CCWA said $20.26 revenue should grow around 44%, and

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:26.840
CAPEX stays at $60 billion to $64 billion. High performance computing was 68% of third-quarter

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:39.260
revenue, and 2 nanometer rows to 8% of wafer revenue from 3% in the second quarter. Gross

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:44.760
Kendall Huang said overseas fab dilution should run close to 2% this year, and widened

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:46.120
to 3-4% later.

00:02:47.263 --> 00:02:53.523
CCWA told analysts TSMC is still discussing Elon Musk's tariff fab, and that the fab has

00:02:53.523 --> 00:02:55.323
got to be run by TSMC.

00:02:55.903 --> 00:03:01.063
Musk had said his companies would build and operate the plant, and that TSMC might sublease

00:03:01.063 --> 00:03:03.443
part of the site but would not run manufacturing.

00:03:04.183 --> 00:03:07.903
Intel is reportedly helping develop the technology that plant would use.

00:03:07.903 --> 00:03:14.383
The information reports TSMC will add a new 3 nanometer fab as AI orders pile up, and

00:03:14.383 --> 00:03:17.583
a Texas fab is under evaluation with no final decision.

00:03:18.627 --> 00:03:21.127
Open-weight models take it apart at the memory shelf.

00:03:21.727 --> 00:03:27.547
Semiconductor Engineering cites a report that a 120 billion parameter model runs on 180

00:03:27.547 --> 00:03:28.527
gigabyte GPU.

00:03:29.207 --> 00:03:35.707
The same note says a 20 billion parameter model can sit in 16 gigabytes and both use MXFP4.

00:03:35.707 --> 00:03:39.907
If the weight file does not fit that shelf, the model does not run there.

00:03:40.507 --> 00:03:44.867
Sherrod Choli of Expedera says publishing the weights lets you host the model yourself,

00:03:45.347 --> 00:03:47.347
so no one vendor owns the next token.

00:03:47.987 --> 00:03:53.347
As of September 2026, he said, the larger open weight models come mainly from Europe or

00:03:53.347 --> 00:03:56.967
Asia, and the field is moving toward trillion parameter models.

00:03:57.527 --> 00:04:00.827
Guillaume Boyette of our terrace says the file is not the recipe.

00:04:01.407 --> 00:04:04.387
Training data, code, and usage rights can stay closed.

00:04:04.387 --> 00:04:12.147
About 250 open-weight models from major companies showed up on hugging face in two years, not counting quantized copies.

00:04:12.787 --> 00:04:19.307
Choli describes distilling a 400-billion-parameter deep-seek C model into an 8-billion-parameter Quinn model,

00:04:19.667 --> 00:04:23.947
and he does not expect 100-billion-parameter models to sweep device benchmarks.

00:04:24.527 --> 00:04:30.727
Thomas Anderson of Synopsis says chip design still needs proprietary data, those public weights do not hold.

00:04:30.727 --> 00:04:36.087
And the piece notes model architectures can change in weeks while silicon takes years.

00:04:36.687 --> 00:04:38.947
Memory fit alone is not useful performance.

00:04:39.427 --> 00:04:43.367
The 80 gigabyte shelf stops being the right machine when the job needs the missing

00:04:43.367 --> 00:04:48.187
data, the missing rights, or a sustained run that merely storing the weights cannot feed.

00:04:49.152 --> 00:04:53.212
On the horizon, a day after packaging capacity was still the open question.

